[JUARFJSX]: 71, n. 205 doubts the identification of "brtson 'grus dbang phyug" - the author of (ID:4720) - as sBal ti jo sras, suggesting, rather that the author could have been a student of Phya pa (ID:3831). In that case, (ID:4720) would be a different work from the one listed by A khu ching shes rab rgya mtsho in his Tho yig ([5RXEUKD9]: 529, No. 11509: sbal ti jo sras kyi 'dul ba).</note></person><person xml:id="person3968"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gzhu ba ston yes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཞུ་བ་སྟོན་ཡེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gzhu pa ston yes</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">3968</idno></person><person xml:id="person6929"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rnal 'byor byang chub seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྣལ་འབྱོར་བྱང་ཆུབ་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rnal 'byor byang seng ge</persName><birth notBefore="1130-01-01" notAfter="1179-12-31">after 1130 before 1179</birth><death notBefore="1234-01-01" notAfter="1259-12-31">after 1234 before 1259</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1356</idno><idno type="APIS">6929</idno><note type="comment">[J5GQTH4E]: 70 gives the dates: ca. 1130-1200.&#13;
